  "# Codegen co-scientist, iteration 24

Iteration 23 asked for `:cfg-liveness` or keep all-vreg forever. This file
does neither. It locates the throw that 23 read as last-uses.

Do not overwrite 04-23.

## The throw

With `back-edge?` rewritten to false, `allocate-without-spills` never
scans count-loop or countdown. `entry-argument-plan` requires
`:mir/argument` as a prefix. Both fixtures started with
`:mir/label :test.label/preheader`. That is `:non-prefix-argument`,
tagged `:spill-required`, so `allocate-with-policy` falls to all-vreg.
Ex-data is not an instruction.

After `lower-phis`, latch values are merge-stored after their defs.
last-uses of the iteration-23 lowered count-loop: `n1@16 acc1@17`, defs
at 14 and 13. The header phi is gone.

## The measurement

Arguments first, preheader label after them, `back-edge?` still false:
both shapes, both targets, policy `:call-live`. Override live
(`pos? @calls`). Test:
`v3-prefix-argument-call-loops-complete-the-scanner`.

Production still `:all-vregs` via the guard
(`v3-call-plus-back-edge-is-routed-to-all-vregs`).

Judah: kotoba-mir **45 tests, 1006 assertions, 0 failures**.

## What this is not

Not cfg-liveness. Not predicate removal. Not amu execution of the
scanner path. amu's count-loop copy was not moved; it still executes
all-vreg. Remove `back-edge?` when that path runs in amu, not against
encodings.

## Pins

Allocator code is still kotoba-mir `ac14016d` / kotoba-native `69e364e`.
This iteration is fixtures + paper + one test.

- kotoba-mir `6ccc30eb4a90548c94bc62a912e91386197a069e` (merge of
  `agent/prefix-arg-loop-scanner`, feature
  `173e04a30276f45537b712e29455be46566227f7`).
  west-pin `0501c1bdd47159c4045630eb0d297ab1b1b384ec`
- amu not moved
- kotoba-native not moved (`69e364edf3154aa8fdf7d87535ca73179b4d2716`)

## Meta-review

- **A fallback tagged :spill-required is not evidence about last-uses.**
  Read `:instruction :problem`.
- **Named Next is a hypothesis.** 23 named cfg-liveness because it
  explained the green. The green was an unstarted scanner.
- **Do not remove `back-edge?` because encodings now complete.** That is
  iteration 22's judgement with a working corpus. The remaining gate is
  amu execution.

